The model weights were trained on the following data:

- Universal NER, English EWT (UNER_English-EWT), CC BY-SA 4.0
  https://github.com/UniversalNER/UNER_English-EWT
  Mayhew et al., "Universal NER: A Gold-Standard Multilingual Named Entity Recognition Benchmark", NAACL 2024.
- GermEval 2014 NER Shared Task data, CC BY 4.0
  https://sites.google.com/site/germeval2014ner/
  Benikova, Biemann, Reznicek, "NoSta-D Named Entity Annotation for German: Guidelines and Dataset", LREC 2014.
- WNUT 2017 Emerging and Rare Entities, CC BY 4.0
  https://github.com/leondz/emerging_entities_17
  Derczynski et al., "Results of the WNUT2017 Shared Task on Novel and Emerging Entity Recognition", 2017.
- Broad Twitter Corpus, CC BY 4.0
  https://github.com/GateNLP/broad_twitter_corpus
  Derczynski, Bontcheva, Roberts, "Broad Twitter Corpus: A Diverse Named Entity Recognition Resource", COLING 2016.
- Sentence templates from Microsoft Presidio Research, MIT License
  https://github.com/microsoft/presidio-research
- Synthetic sentences generated by tarnkappe/data.py using the Faker library (MIT License).

model/vectors.npz is derived from the word vectors in spaCy's en_core_web_md and
de_core_news_md packages (MIT License), whose vectors Explosion publishes as CC0:
"Explosion Vectors (OSCAR 2109 + Wikipedia + OpenSubtitles + WMT News Crawl)" and
"Explosion fastText Vectors (cbow, OSCAR Common Crawl + Wikipedia)". https://spacy.io

model/first_names.txt is a list of first names sampled from the Faker library (MIT License).
